/-! # Cohomological Brown representability on the constructible localizing hull

Source: blueprint `theorem-exceptional-inverse-image` (3), in its well-generated form.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-adic-localizing-cohomological-representability)
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits
open CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.Opposite
open scoped CategoryTheory.Obj CategoryTheory.Functor

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.CondensedRing

open Scheme

variable (Λ : Sheaf (coherentTopology Profinite.{u}) Ab.{u + 1})
  [MonObj Λ] [IsCommMonObj Λ] (ℓ : ℕ) [Fact ℓ.Prime]
  {k : Type u} [Field k] [Fact (ringChar k).Prime] [Fact (ringChar k ≠ ℓ)]
  (X : Over (Spec (.of k)))
  [LocallyOfFiniteType X.hom] [QuasiCompact X.hom] [IsSeparated X.hom]
  (hΛ : IsEllAdicCoefficient ℓ Λ inferInstance)

include ℓ k hΛ

-- The more general argument below retains every binder of the assigned statement.
set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false in

/-- Brown representability on the localizing hull of adic constructible complexes.

Source: blueprint `theorem-exceptional-inverse-image` (3), `det-existence-localizing.proof.md` (3);
Neeman, *On the derived category of sheaves on a manifold*, Theorem 0.2;
Krause, *Localization theory for triangulated categories*, Theorems 7.2.1 and 5.1.1.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-adic-localizing-cohomological-representability)

Proof: the ambient category of module objects is Grothendieck abelian, so its unbounded derived
category is well generated. Bounded constructible complexes form an essentially small category.
Indeed, stratifications, pro-etale covers, finite ranks, and presentation matrices form small
data. For each fixed choice of these data, the adjoints of the local presentation isomorphisms
embed a realizing module into a fixed product of direct images of the prescribed local cokernels.
The map is monic because exact pullback to the covering members of all strata kills its kernel,
and these restrictions jointly detect zero sheaves. The module category is well-powered, so
domains of subobjects of each fixed product form an essentially small class. The small union over
the local data is essentially small. For a fixed cohomological interval, induct on its length
using truncation triangles: each next extension is classified by an ambient Hom set. The union
over the integer endpoints is still small (`lemma-hypotheses-brown-representability--5`). Choose a
small skeleton S. The displayed hull is exactly the localizing subcategory generated by S, by its
intersection universal property. Its proved countable-coproduct idempotent splitting and
retract-closure instances also give the thick-subcategory convention for localizing subcategories
used by Krause. A localizing subcategory generated by a set in a well-generated category is well
generated (Krause 7.2.1). In detail choose an uncountable regular cardinal for which the ambient
category is well generated and every object of S is alpha-compact; the alpha-localizing closure of S
is a small family of alpha-small perfect generators of the hull. The solution-set part of
perfect-generator Brown's construction (Krause 5.1.1) supplies a small weakly universal family of
H-elements; this remains isolated in `setGeneratedDerived_cohomological_solutionSet`. The final
passage from a solution set to a representation is proved here: take a universal coproduct element,
kill its kernel endomorphisms by a cofiber, and split the resulting idempotent. This argument needs
no compactness of S or cohomological bound on the base field. Small means universe u+1 throughout,
including the skeleton, Hom sets and values of H, so no larger indexing universe is required.
-/
theorem ellAdic_localizing_cohomological_isRepresentable
    (H : (boundedConstructibleLocalizingClosure Λ X.left).FullSubcategoryᵒᵖ ⥤
      AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}) [H.IsHomological]
    (hH : ∀ I : Type (u + 1), PreservesLimitsOfShape (Discrete I) H) :
    (H ⋙ forget AddCommGrpCat).IsRepresentable := by
  have : IsLocallyNoetherian X.left := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian X.hom
  have : CompactSpace X.left := QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace X.hom
  let R := condensedRingObj Λ X.left
  have hheart : ObjectProperty.EssentiallySmall.{u + 1}
      (IsConstructibleModuleObject R) :=
    constructibleModuleObjects_essentiallySmall X.left R
  let P := ObjectProperty.isoClosure (IsConstructibleModuleObject R)
  have hbounded : ObjectProperty.EssentiallySmall.{u + 1} (boundedConstructible R) := by
    have := DerivedCategory.bounded_homologyProperty_essentiallySmall P
    apply ObjectProperty.EssentiallySmall.of_le
      (Q := DerivedCategory.TStructure.t.bounded ⊓ DerivedCategory.homologyProperty P)
    intro K hK
    exact ⟨hK.1, fun n ↦ ObjectProperty.le_isoClosure _ _ (hK.2 n)⟩
  apply cohomological_isRepresentable_of_solutionSet H hH
  refine setGeneratedDerived_cohomological_solutionSet (boundedConstructible R)
    (boundedConstructibleLocalizingClosure Λ X.left)
    (boundedConstructible_le_localizingClosure Λ X.left) ?_ H hH
  intro Q hQ hi ht hc
  let := hi
  let := ht
  let := hc
  exact boundedConstructibleLocalizingClosure_le Λ X.left Q hQ

end AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.CondensedRing
